{
  "_doc": "Angles in degrees. Absolute 0 = down, +90 = forward (side view) or outward (front view). spine.lean tilts the whole body forward; chest/neck/head are relative. arm.shoulder is relative to the torso's downward line, elbow flexes forward (0..160), knee flexes backward (0..160), ankle is the foot's angle from the ground, not the shin: 0 = flat with toes forward (side view) or outward (front view), + lifts the toes (-180..180). headView: front | side. arm.hand: fist | out (thumb away from body) | in (thumb toward body) | point (like out, one long finger, shorter grouped fingers). mouth: 1 (slit), 2 (arch), 3 (wide shout). Poses are side view only; the front view is derived from them by the renderer (view: front): near = picture-right, far = picture-left. arm.out / leg.out (drawn parts): the whole arm or leg turned out of the paper, + = away from the body sideways (-90..90); side view shortens it by cos(out), front view shows its sideways reach.",
